# Convergence — bounded consumer validation

AC-01..04 APPROVED. All 28 pending original scenarios received concrete execution and criterion-specific semantic review. The nine skills now have 36/36 technical and 54/54 total approved criteria, scoped to the identified consumers. Existing 26 approved requirement objects and all original skill contracts are unchanged.

16 model tests, seven process/filesystem tests, four isolated read attempts and the complete graphical interaction test passed. The minimum-size Quit clipping was corrected after an observed failure. All 42 governance tests passed; six methods passed on an independently copied package. Final copied-package validation is recorded separately after finalization, without a self-referential receipt.

Review: docs/validation/skill-consumers-20261101/review.md. Mapping: matrix.json. Exact predecessors and failed trials are retained. Product implementation and independent product acceptance remain separate; no new agent trial, commit or external publication.
